===Miguel's Journal===
{{Transcript|text=
!! WARNING !!

Database corrupted. Partial entries recovered.
}}

====Hello, World!====
{{Transcript|text=
It's been real hard being on my own since the bombs dropped. But the Responders... they have it figure out. They got someone working on vaccines and medicines and stuff, and they even turn regular people into volunteers.

I took all their survival training programs and passed with aces. So now I'm a Responder too. Nifty, right?
}}

====The Cause====
{{Transcript|text=
The Scorchbeasts scare me more than anything. It's why I joined the Responders. I knew I couldn't live alone anymore, and they have stuff figured out.

I just wish maybe they got along better with the Brotherhood. It's not us or them, it's all of us together. It's a shame.
}}

====Programming Again====
{{Transcript|text=
I used to be a programmer before the bombs fell, and well. Guess what?

... I program robots now, too. I mean, it's important work. I get it. I can help out in the lab, too with other programmers and it's good to have company.

They said they'd let me do some outdoors survival orienteering for new Responders though, so I'm looking forward to that.
}}

====Hope in Flatwoods====
{{Transcript|text=
I'm helping a couple of Responders set up a base out in the [[Flatwoods]]{{sic}} for a bit. They think a bunch of survivors will start getting processed there, so I'm goint to set up camps.

I could do this forever. Camping under the stars and helping people out at the same time is the dream, you know?
}}

====Mr. Fluffy====
{{Transcript|text=
We're actually making progress! Oh man. I even got myself a new Protectron bodyguard today.

It has an attitude problem though, but that's what happens when you put a bunch of parts together randomly, sometimes. I called him [[Mr. Fluffy]], which really irritated it for some reason. "Error: Metallic surface is not fluffy. Error: Does not compute."

I've seen it before, so I'm going to need to write a program that resets their brains. This might take a while.
}}

====Despair in Flatwoods====
{{Transcript|text=
Flatwoods is... rough. So many refugees, not enough Responders. I'm going to start making advanced training courses for Volunteers because... there aren't enough of us to train everyone individually.

Good news though! I met someone on the road between the airport and Flatwoods... glad to have someone who will keep me company. It's a long walk and Mr. Fluffy - the robot - is not a good exercise partner.
}}

====Reset Program====
{{Transcript|text=
I wrote a program that will reset my protectron's brain to settings that are a little more conventional for a robot instead of standing next to me, day and night, forever.

Which is, I gotta say, really ruining my sex life right about now.
}}

====Peace, Appalachia====
{{Transcript|text=
I should have signed up for the [[Vault-Tec Corporation|Vault-Tec]] stuff, but the thought of being in a tin can for a hundred years was too terrifying. But here it is. Every day more of us die. I haven't seen a refugee in... too long.

If I'm goint to get ripped to shreds, I'm doing it with a pot of Delbert's chili, in the woods, and under the beautiful stars. I refused to die in an office! But... I need to wait for Garry. Then we'll go together.
}}

====This is it.====
{{Transcript|text=
All I've wanted to do since the bombs fell was help people and explore what's left of nature.

But... he's dead, Maria. Garry died this morning. It was just an accident. One of those things broke though the gate. I already buried him up on the hill with the others...

What's the point here with any of this if we can't even protect ourselves?

I'm going to my camp, and I'll take my robot. I just need to figure things out.
}}
